===Glyph origin===
{{Han etym}}
{{Han compound|首|卩|ls=p|c1=head|c2=kneeling posture}} – head of a kneeling person, emphasising “head”.

{{lang|zh|頁}} and {{och-l|首}} were originally the same pictographic character with the same meaning of “head”, and the graphical difference was that {{lang|zh|頁}} also included the body in addition to the head of the person.

{{lang|zh|頁}} was later used as an alternative popular form of {{zh-l|*葉|leaf; page}} to mean “sheet; page (of paper)”, which is its main meaning today.

The original sense of “head” is preserved in the radical {{lang|zh|頁}}, which is used in characters such as {{zh-l|*頭|head}} and {{zh-l|*頸|neck}}.

